guide forever/collectibles/mounts/neutral/warlock-dreadsteed
title Warlock Dreadsteed
category Class
folder Warlock
keywords Summon Dreadsteed, Mor'zul Bloodbringer, Rage of Blood, Raging Beast's Blood, Wildeyes, Gorzeeki Wildeyes, Case of Blood, Lord Banehollow, Shadowy Potion, Taint of Shadow, Jaedenar, Shadow Hold, Ulathek the Traitor, The Traitor's Heart, Xorothian Stardust, Ur'dan, Bell of Dethmoora, Wheel of the Black March, Doomsday Candle, Arcanite, Imp Delivery, J'eevee, Imp in a Jar, Scholomance, Ras Frostwhisper, Dreadsteed of Xoroth, J'eevee's Jar, Black Lodestone, Xorothian Glyphs, Circle of Greater Summoning, Dread Guard, Xorothian Dreadsteed, Lord Hel'nurath, Immol'thar, Dire Maul, Crescent Key, Warlock, class mount
reward spell 23161 "Summon Dreadsteed"
why Your epic mount at 60, summoned anywhere: no epic horse to buy and no 1,000g Journeyman Riding needed.
class Warlock
levels 60-60
zone Burning Steppes

# Summon Dreadsteed: the twelve quests of the Dreadsteed chain, routed in
# full. Your demon trainer's hand-off to Mor'zul Bloodbringer (7562: Spackle
# Thornberry, Stormwind; Jubahl Corpseseeker, Ironforge; Kurgul, Orgrimmar;
# Martha Strain, Undercity), Rage of Blood (7563, 30 Raging Beast's Blood from
# the Winterspring owlbeasts) and Wildeyes (7564, the Case of Blood to Gorzeeki
# Wildeyes beside Mor'zul). Then two branches: Mor'zul's Bell of Dethmoora
# (7626, 10 Elixirs of Shadow Power), Wheel of the Black March (7627, 6 Large
# Brilliant Shards and 25 Dark Iron Ore) and Doomsday Candle (7628, 35 Black
# Dragonscales), then Gorzeeki's Arcanite (7630, 3 Arcanite Bars); and
# Gorzeeki's Lord Banehollow (7623, Shadowy Potions through Jaedenar in
# Felwood), Ulathek the Traitor (7624, The Traitor's Heart) and Xorothian
# Stardust (7625, bought from Ur'dan). Both join at Imp Delivery (7629, pre
# 7625 and 7630: the Imp in a Jar at the alchemy lab in the Scholomance), then
# Dreadsteed of Xoroth (7631, Mor'zul's Instructions: the ritual in Dire Maul
# West with J'eevee's Jar, the Black Lodestone and the Xorothian Glyphs), and
# the Dreadsteed Spirit binds the horse to you.
# An Imp's Request (Impsy), Niby's Shard of the Green Flame and Daio's Tome of
# Sacrifice are not part of this chain.
# Material counts are Forever's (quests.json and Forever's quest pages: 10
# elixirs, 6 shards and 25 ore, 35 scales, 3 bars), the same as the Classic
# era reference class guide asks for.
# Prices (Forever's item data, Gorzeeki's and Ur'dan's goods): Shadowy Potion
# 6 gold, Xorothian Stardust 150, J'eevee's Jar 150, Black Lodestone 50,
# Xorothian Glyphs 50: about 420 gold with three potions, before materials.
# Three potions, not two: one to walk in, one after Ulathek (the fight trick
# clicks the first off), and a spare for the 20-minute limit; one reference
# buys six. The jar, lodestone and glyphs are not used up: a warlock who owns
# them can run your ritual and save you 250 gold.
# Drops: the owlbeasts (53-58, all five kinds, none elite) drop the blood
# about one time in three and respawn in five and a half minutes (items.json,
# quest notes): about ninety kills. Black Dragonscales are skinned from the
# black dragonkin of the Burning Steppes at a few percent each (Flamescale
# Wyrmkin about 7%). Dark Iron Ore: Dark Iron Deposits (Mining 230) in the
# Burning Steppes and Blackrock Depths, or the golems there (about 13%).
# The ritual (Classic wiki, quest notes): kill Immol'thar first, his dais is
# the circle. J'eevee sets out the Bell (heals and restores mana of warlocks
# in the party), the Wheel (absorbs damage on the party) and the Candle (burns
# anyone outside the party, so the imps die fast). Imps come in waves with
# about ten Dread Guards (elite felguards); the nodes sag, tilt and sound when
# they fail, and the Black Lodestone recharges one in a 3-second cast that any
# damage interrupts, for a Soul Shard each: 10-15 shards. Any warlock in the
# party with a Lodestone can recharge. All three down ends the ritual; one
# still up keeps it going even through a wipe. About six minutes and nine
# symbols later a red vortex closes the circle. The Glyphs then call the
# Xorothian Dreadsteed (62, elite); at half health Lord Hel'nurath (62) joins.
# Any warlock who finished the chain up to here can bind the spirit while it
# lasts. No source sets a minimum of three players: the ritual needs a party
# of five (the Imp Delivery fails in a raid group, player reports) with
# someone free to watch each of the three nodes.
# Places inside the dungeons have no spawns in our data: their goals point at
# the Scholomance entrance (Caer Darrow 69.7,73.2, Forever's dungeon data) and
# at Dire Maul West's door (60.3,30.2: one reference guide's door step and a Forever
# dungeon guide's 60.3,31.8 agree; our data has only the Dire Maul gate,
# 59.2,45.1, at the foot of the ruins, a long walk south of the wing).
# Materials nothing drops (elixirs, shards, bars) point at the auctioneers of
# Stormwind and Orgrimmar.
# ASSUMED: The ritual and fights run as in Classic (Classic flow; Forever's data has no play reports past the level-30 beta cap). In-game check: node recharging, the Dread Guard waves and Hel'nurath at half health.
# Riding: Summon Dreadsteed needs no Journeyman Riding. Forever client
# 1.60.1.70532 (wago.tools): its mount type's MountCapability asks for Riding 0
# and gives 100% speed; PlayerCondition 31504 asks only for the Warlock quest
# "Dreadsteed of Xoroth" (7631).
# Sources: Forever's quest data (quests.json, npcs.json, items.json, the
# codex's item costs); Forever's client tables for the spell; the quest notes
# (data/local/mechanics); the Classic wiki's Dreadsteed questline page for
# the ritual; the reference class guides for the order.

step Mor'zul Bloodbringer (Stormwind)
  only Human
  zone Stormwind City
  tip At 60 Spackle Thornberry, the demon trainer in the Slaughtered Lamb, sends you to Mor'zul Bloodbringer in the Burning Steppes.
  level 60
  accept 7562 npc 5520                -- Spackle Thornberry

step Mor'zul Bloodbringer (Ironforge)
  only Gnome
  zone Ironforge
  tip At 60 Jubahl Corpseseeker, the demon trainer in Ironforge, sends you to Mor'zul Bloodbringer in the Burning Steppes.
  level 60
  accept 7562 npc 6382                -- Jubahl Corpseseeker

step Mor'zul Bloodbringer (Orgrimmar)
  only Orc,Troll
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip At 60 Kurgul, the demon trainer in the Cleft of Shadow, sends you to Mor'zul Bloodbringer in the Burning Steppes.
  level 60
  accept 7562 npc 5815                -- Kurgul

step Mor'zul Bloodbringer (Undercity)
  only Undead
  zone Undercity
  tip At 60 Martha Strain, the demon trainer in the Magic Quarter, sends you to Mor'zul Bloodbringer in the Burning Steppes.
  level 60
  accept 7562 npc 5753                -- Martha Strain

step Mor'zul Bloodbringer
  zone Burning Steppes
  tip Mor'zul Bloodbringer and his goblin Gorzeeki Wildeyes camp on the hill across the road from the Altar of Storms, in the far north-west of the Burning Steppes, west of Blackrock Mountain. The chain is long: about 420 gold in Gorzeeki's and Ur'dan's goods, a pile of crafted materials, the Scholomance and Dire Maul. Start buying or gathering the materials of the next steps now.
  turnin 7562                         -- Mor'zul Bloodbringer
  accept 7563

step Raging Beast's Blood
  zone Winterspring
  tip Every owlbeast of Winterspring (level 53-58, none elite) drops the blood about one time in three: about ninety kills for thirty. Owl Wing Thicket, in the north-east, and the Hidden Grove's surroundings are packed with them, and they respawn in five and a half minutes.
  collect 18590 x30 quest 7563.1      -- Raging Beast's Blood

step Wildeyes
  zone Burning Steppes
  tip Back to Mor'zul: he gives you the Case of Blood for Gorzeeki beside him. Then Mor'zul asks for the bell, the wheel and the candle, and Gorzeeki sends you to Lord Banehollow in Jaedenar: buy three Shadowy Potions from him for that trip (6 gold each: one to walk in, one after Ulathek, and a spare in case one runs out) and bring 150 gold for the stardust.
  turnin 7563                         -- Mor'zul Bloodbringer
  accept 7564                         -- he gives you the Case of Blood
  turnin 7564                         -- Gorzeeki Wildeyes
  accept 7626                         -- Mor'zul Bloodbringer: Bell of Dethmoora
  accept 7627                         -- Mor'zul Bloodbringer: Wheel of the Black March
  accept 7628                         -- Mor'zul Bloodbringer: Doomsday Candle
  accept 7623                         -- Gorzeeki Wildeyes: Lord Banehollow
  buy 18802 x3 npc 14437              -- Shadowy Potion, from Gorzeeki

step The ritual pieces
  tip Gorzeeki wants 10 Elixirs of Shadow Power (Alchemy: 3 Ghost Mushrooms and a Crystal Vial each), 6 Large Brilliant Shards (Enchanting: disenchant level 51+ blue items), 25 Dark Iron Ore (Mining 230: the Dark Iron Deposits of the Burning Steppes and Blackrock Depths) and 35 Black Dragonscales (Skinning: the black dragonkin of the Burning Steppes, a few percent a kill, best from the Flamescale Wyrmkin). Make or gather what your professions allow and buy the rest at the Auction House; it can take a while to find 35 scales.
  collect 9264 x10 quest 7626.1 @61.2,71.3 map 1453 live only Alliance -- Elixir of Shadow Power: the Auction House
  collect 9264 x10 quest 7626.1 @55.9,62.7 map 1454 only Horde -- Elixir of Shadow Power: the Auction House
  collect 14344 x6 quest 7627.1 @61.2,71.3 map 1453 live only Alliance -- Large Brilliant Shard: the Auction House
  collect 14344 x6 quest 7627.1 @55.9,62.7 map 1454 only Horde -- Large Brilliant Shard: the Auction House
  collect 11370 x25 quest 7627.2      -- Dark Iron Ore
  collect 15416 x35 quest 7628.1      -- Black Dragonscale

step Arcanite
  zone Burning Steppes
  tip Hand the three pieces to Gorzeeki. He then wants 3 Arcanite Bars for the Black Lodestone: alchemists transmute them (an Arcane Crystal and a Thorium Bar each, on a long cooldown); everyone else buys them.
  turnin 7626                         -- Gorzeeki Wildeyes
  turnin 7627                         -- Gorzeeki Wildeyes
  turnin 7628                         -- Gorzeeki Wildeyes
  accept 7630
  collect 12360 x3 quest 7630.1 @61.2,71.3 map 1453 live only Alliance -- Arcanite Bar: the Auction House
  collect 12360 x3 quest 7630.1 @55.9,62.7 map 1454 only Horde -- Arcanite Bar: the Auction House
  turnin 7630                         -- Gorzeeki Wildeyes

step Lord Banehollow
  zone Felwood
  tip Jaedenar lies just south of Bloodvenom Post in western Felwood, west of the road; of its two caves, Shadow Hold is the northern one, further up the hill. Drink a Shadowy Potion at its mouth: for 20 minutes the Shadow Council there treat you as one of their own (Taint of Shadow). The oozes in the red pool and the succubus Rakaiah beyond them still attack: hug the wall past them. Go down past the second, red pool, up the ramp and across two bridges to Lord Banehollow, a great winged dreadlord at the back. He talks to you only while the potion lasts.
  goto 35.4,58.6 "Shadow Hold"
  turnin 7623 @35.9,44.4              -- Lord Banehollow
  accept 7624

step Ulathek the Traitor
  tip Ulathek waits in a small side room up a bridge you passed on the way down. Speak to him and he and four guards attack (all level 57, none elite): let your voidwalker hold the guards and burn Ulathek, sacrificing it if you must. Or click off your Taint of Shadow aura to start the fight, kill Ulathek, then drink another potion: the guards stop at once. Take his heart back to Lord Banehollow with a potion active.
  kill 14523 optional                 -- Ulathek
  collect 18719 quest 7624.1          -- The Traitor's Heart
  turnin 7624 @35.9,44.4              -- Lord Banehollow
  accept 7625

step Xorothian Stardust
  tip Ur'dan, beside Lord Banehollow, sells the Xorothian Stardust for 150 gold. He deals with you only while a Shadowy Potion is active.
  buy 18687 npc 14522                 -- Xorothian Stardust, from Ur'dan

step Imp Delivery
  zone Burning Steppes
  tip Back to Gorzeeki with the stardust; with the Arcanite also done he gives you the Imp in a Jar for the Scholomance. Put a group of five together now: a party, not a raid group.
  buy 18687 npc 14522                 -- Xorothian Stardust, from Ur'dan
  turnin 7625                         -- Gorzeeki Wildeyes
  accept 7629

step The Scholomance
  zone Western Plaguelands
  tip The Scholomance (level 58-60, a group of five) lies under Caer Darrow, the island town in the south-east of the Western Plaguelands: someone needs the Skeleton Key or a rogue to open the door. Fight down to Ras Frostwhisper's room and use the Imp in a Jar at the alchemy lab tables to the right: J'eevee makes the parchment. You need not kill Ras, but it only counts at this lab and only in a party.
  complete 7629 @69.7,73.2 group 5    -- Use the Imp in a Jar at the alchemy lab inside

step Dreadsteed of Xoroth
  zone Burning Steppes
  tip Back to Gorzeeki, then Mor'zul hands you his instructions. Buy J'eevee's Jar (150 gold), the Black Lodestone (50) and the Xorothian Glyphs (50) from Gorzeeki; a warlock friend who owns them can bring theirs instead. Every other warlock who will recharge the nodes needs a Lodestone of their own. Carry 15 or more Soul Shards.
  turnin 7629                         -- Gorzeeki Wildeyes
  accept 7631                         -- Mor'zul Bloodbringer
  buy 18663 npc 14437                 -- J'eevee's Jar, 150 gold
  buy 18629 npc 14437                 -- Black Lodestone, 50 gold
  buy 18670 npc 14437                 -- Xorothian Glyphs, 50 gold

step Into Dire Maul West
  zone Feralas
  tip Dire Maul stands in the ruins of central Feralas: from the gate at the foot of the ruins, walk up through the outer courtyards to the west wing's door at the north end. That door and an inner door need the Crescent Key (it drops from Pusillin in Dire Maul East) or a rogue with 300 Lockpicking. Bring a party of five. Lower Immol'thar's shield by killing the guardians of the five pylons (two stand in his own room), then kill Immol'thar: his dais is the summoning circle. Rest and rebuff before you start.
  kill 11496 @60.3,30.2 group 5       -- Immol'thar, inside the west wing

step The ritual
  tip Stand on the dais and use J'eevee's Jar: J'eevee sets out the Bell, the Wheel and the Candle. The Bell heals warlocks, the Wheel shields the party, the Candle burns the imps: ignore the imps and kill the Dread Guards (elite felguards, about ten, sometimes two at once); Banish or Enslave helps. Give one player each node to watch: when one sags, tilts and sounds, a warlock with a Lodestone recharges it, a 3-second cast that any hit breaks (a Soul Shard each), so keep attackers off them. If all three fail, the ritual ends and you start again; while one stands it survives even a wipe. After about six minutes nine symbols glow and a red vortex closes the circle: walk out and the remaining demons vanish at its edge. Rest, then use the Xorothian Glyphs. Kill the Xorothian Dreadsteed (level 62, elite); at half health Lord Hel'nurath joins, a hard hitter who knocks you back. Speak to the Dreadsteed Spirit: every warlock in the party who is on this quest can bind it.
  use 18663 @60.3,30.2                -- J'eevee's Jar, on Immol'thar's dais
  use 18670 @60.3,30.2                -- Xorothian Glyphs, once the circle is complete
  kill 14502 quest 7631.1 @60.3,30.2 group 5 -- Xorothian Dreadsteed
  turnin 7631 @60.3,30.2              -- Dreadsteed Spirit: Summon Dreadsteed
